// Telemetry heartbeat for the Real-Time Dashboard: CPU samples per target and bin. CPU samples arrive every
// 10 seconds (15 for Azure SQL Database), so a steady line means a target is reporting and a gap means it isn't
// (the "Tables" table in https://learn.microsoft.com/fabric/database/hub/microsoft-sql-query-performance-monitoring-telemetry,
// checked 2026-10-21). Runs after Live.Prelude.kql. Rules applied: 1 (filter on SampleTimeUTC first), 7 (samples
// per bin, which read as time), and an aggregation as the row limit (rule 10). Sample counts aren't counters, so
// summing them per target doesn't mix counter values from different instances (rule 4).
SqlServerCPUUtilization
| where SampleTimeUTC between (_start .. _end)
| where ResourceGroup =~ _rg
| extend Target = _target(ResourceType, ResourceName)
| where isnotempty(Target)
| summarize Samples = count() by Target, Bucket = bin(SampleTimeUTC, _bin)
| order by Bucket asc
